course: dictionary
lesson: 6522
title: Family words: nephew
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A nephew is a family word. Your nephew is the son of your brother or sister. In «Chloe's aunt got a call that sounded exactly like her crying nephew», the aunt has a nephew, so he must be a son of her brother or sister.
explain: The word can also be wider. Your nephew can be the son of your husband's or wife's brother or sister. So family words can reach beyond your own blood family, through the people you marry.
explain: Context gives more clues. The word «crying» and the phrase «asking for money» show the nephew is a young person, and a scammer copied his voice to trick the aunt. Ask yourself who the child's parent is, and whether that parent is your sibling or your partner's sibling. If so, the child is your nephew.
fact: A nephew is the son of your brother or sister.
fact: A nephew can also be the son of your husband's or wife's brother or sister.
fact: In a family tree, a nephew is one generation below you.
fact: Phrases to know: «my nephew», «nephews and nieces», and «great-nephew».
fact: Check a family word by asking whose child he is, then which family member that person is to you.
exercise: What is a nephew? | A daughter of your brother | A grandad | A teacher | *The son of your brother or sister
exercise: In a family tree, where is a nephew compared with you? | *One generation below you | Above you, one generation up | Far away from the tree | Level with you, in the same generation
exercise: Copy the word from the sentence that means the son of your brother or sister. | voice | aunt | scammers | *nephew
test: Your husband's sister's son is your ___. | cousin | *nephew | friend | aunt
test: Ravi's sister has a baby boy. The baby is Ravi's ___. | friend | cousin | *nephew | niece
exam: Which statement is true? | A nephew is a type of cake | *A nephew is the son of your brother or sister | A nephew is your parent | A nephew is always older than you
